    native_build_shard_timeout_reported_as_crash_2026_11_11, P2, fix-implemented-verification-pending, "native-build shard worker killed at --timeout deadline is reported as CRASH", src/app/cli/native_build_main.spl, 1248, test/01_unit/compiler/driver/hir_shard_timeout_state_spec.spl, 2026-11-11, 2026-11-11, true

bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    native_build_shard_timeout_reported_as_crash_2026_11_11, 0, "2026-11-11 root cause: reap state was 'elif code < 0: CRASH' and a deadline reap leaves code = -2 (still running). Fix: TIMEOUT added to the terminal set (driver_hir_recovery.spl hir_shard_recovery_terminal); new pure classifiers hir_shard_reap_deadline_hit_v1(polled, timeout_ms, elapsed_ms) and hir_shard_reap_state_v1(blocked, code, finished, deadline_hit); the reap loop records deadline_hit and seals TIMEOUT, printing status=TIMEOUT (deadline <n>s). Label-only: exit code, failed_workers, block and replacement logic unchanged (code still < 0). Not changed: the HIR-owner path (own profile deadline) and the per-file/fork child seals (native_file_unit_loop_v1, native_mir_fork_v1), which have no deadline signal. Spec test/01_unit/compiler/driver/hir_shard_timeout_state_spec.spl red 0/5 -> green 5/5; hir_terminal_idempotent_spec 3/3 stays green. Native verification pending a stage3 run with --timeout."
